---
/*
 * `/data/ceo-tenure` — how long Korean listed-company CEOs have held the seat.
 * (seoulmarkets.com/data/ceo-tenure)
 *
 * ── Why this page (2026-10-12 15:3x · 5번) ───────────────────────────
 *   세 번째 데이터 지면이다. `check-쥔자료에-안쓴축이-있나.mjs` 가 내놓은 186개에서 골랐다.
 *   `korea-executives-tape.json` 은 2,769개 회사의 대표 3,589명을 담고 있는데
 *   `tenure` 칸을 쓴 지면이 하나도 없었다.
 *
 *   고른 까닭 — **그 지면에만 있는 수**가 나온다.
 *   ```
 *     중앙값 9년 · 가장 긴 것 55년
 *     20년 넘게 앉은 «자리» 839 — 잰 것의 27.4%
 *     상근 중앙 10년 / 비상근 중앙 2년   ← 다섯 배가 넘는다
 *     ⬜ 못 잰 것 378 (10.5%) · ⚠ 설립일보다 길어 따로 센 것 147
 *   ```
 *   「한국 기업은 오너 중심이라 대표가 오래 간다」가 통념인데,
 *   잰 것의 **23.3%는 3년도 안 됐다.** 분포가 양쪽 끝으로 갈라진다.
 *
 * ── 🔴 하마터면 기사와 어긋날 뻔했다 (2026-10-12 15:5x) ──────────────
 *   지면을 다 짓고 빌드한 뒤에야 **우리 기사가 이미 있는 것을 봤다** —
 *   `/article/korea-ceo-tenure-eleven-year-median`.
 *   「안 쓴 축」 자가 **데이터 지면만 세고 기사는 안 셌다.**
 *
 *   그 기사는 **설립일보다 긴 재임 148건을 걸러냈는데 내 첫 자는 안 걸렀다.**
 *   그래서 내 지면의 맨 앞 수가 「가장 긴 것 58년」이었다 —
 *   **기사가 이미 의심스럽다고 밝힌 바로 그 줄이다.**
 *   ⇒ 같은 거름을 자에 넣었다. 그러자 거른 수가 **147** 로 나왔다(기사 148).
 *     서로 다른 자료·다른 자로 재서 둘이 맞았다 — 이것이 견줌이다.
 *   ⭐ 강령 ⑤ 「한 곳을 고치면 인용한 곳까지 따라간다」의 **거꾸로 꼴**이다.
 *     남이 먼저 고친 것을 내가 안 보고 거친 수로 낼 뻔했다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ What this page must not become ────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 「오래 앉는 것이 좋다/나쁘다」를 말하지 않는다. 얼마나 오래인가까지다.
 * ⛔ 다른 나라와 견주지 않는다 — **우리가 안 쟀다.** 남의 수를 옮겨 적지 않는다.
 * ⛔ 평균을 앞에 내지 않는다 — 평균이 규범이 되면 나침반이 아니라 압박이 된다.
 * ⛔ 같은 이름을 한 사람으로 합치지 않는다 — 생년이 없다. 겸직은 아예 안 센다.
 * ⛔ 못 잰 378명을 0으로 채우지 않는다. 지면에 그대로 적는다.
 * ⛔ English only — 사장님 2026-08-05 「우리 손님은 영어권이다. 화면에 한국어를 안 낸다」.
 * ⛔ Numbers come from src/data/ceo-tenure.json, never typed by hand.
 * 🔴 Astro frontmatter (between the `---`) is TypeScript. JSX breaks the build.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../consts';
import facts from '../../data/ceo-tenure.json';
import BuyBar from '../../components/BuyBar.astro';

const f = facts as any;
const N = (n: number | null | undefined) =>
  n == null ? '—' : Number(n).toLocaleString('en-GB');
const pct = (x: number | null | undefined, d = 1) =>
  x == null ? '—' : `${(Number(x) * 100).toFixed(d)}%`;
const 해 = (y: number | null | undefined) => {
  if (y == null) return '—';
  const n = Number(y);
  if (n < 1) return `${Math.round(n * 12)} months`;
  return `${n % 1 === 0 ? n : n.toFixed(1)} years`;
};

const 칸 = Array.isArray(f.칸) ? f.칸 : [];
const 오래 = Array.isArray(f.오래) ? f.오래 : [];
const 가장큰칸 = 칸.reduce(
  (a: any, b: any) => ((b?.수 ?? 0) > (a?.수 ?? 0) ? b : a),
  칸[0] ?? null,
);
/* 3년 미만 — 「오래 앉는다」의 반대쪽. ⛔ 고르지 않고 아래 두 칸을 더한다 */
const 삼년밑 = 칸.slice(0, 2).reduce((s: number, c: any) => s + (c?.수 ?? 0), 0);
const 삼년밑몫 = f.잰수 ? 삼년밑 / f.잰수 : null;
const 못잰몫 = f.대표수 ? f.못잰수 / f.대표수 : null;
const 스물몫 = f.잰수 ? f.스물넘은수 / f.잰수 : null;
const 거른보기 = Array.isArray(f.거른보기) ? f.거른보기 : [];

const title = 'How long Korea’s listed-company CEOs have held the seat';
const description =
  `Across ${N(f.회사수)} listed Korean companies, the median chief executive has held the `
  + `seat for ${해(f.분위?.중앙)}; ${N(f.스물넘은수)} have held it twenty years or more. `
  + `${N(f.못잰수)} filings did not state a tenure we could read.`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical={`${SITE_URL}/data/ceo-tenure`}>
  <article class="wrap">
    <h1>{title}</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      Korean annual reports state, for each registered executive, how long that person has
      held the position. We read that field for <b>{N(f.대표수)} chief-executive seats across
      {' '}{N(f.회사수)} listed companies</b> — seats, not people, because a company can
      register more than one. The median is {해(f.분위?.중앙)}. The longest we are willing to
      print is {해(f.분위?.최대)}. {N(f.못잰수)} filings — {pct(못잰몫)} of them — carried no
      figure we could read, and a further {N(f.거른수)} stated a tenure longer than the
      company has existed. Neither group is filled in with a zero; both are counted and
      reported below.
    </p>

    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><b>{해(f.분위?.중앙)}</b><span>median tenure</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>{N(f.스물넘은수)}</b><span>held the seat 20 years or more</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>{해(f.분위?.최대)}</b><span>longest tenure that survives our checks</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>{N(f.못잰수)}</b><span>tenure not stated or unreadable</span></div>
    </div>

    <h2>The rows we set aside</h2>
    <p>
      {N(f.거른수)} seats report a tenure longer than their company has existed — a chief
      executive of fifty-plus years at a firm incorporated more recently than that. The
      usual explanation is mundane: a company is re-incorporated, renamed or spun out, the
      incorporation date resets, and the filed tenure carries over service at the earlier
      entity. We cannot tell which rows are that and which are an error, so we take them out
      of the distribution and <b>print the count instead of deleting them</b>. A further
      {' '}{N(f.나이모름)} seats sit at companies whose incorporation date we do not hold;
      those we leave in, because we have no basis to doubt them.
    </p>
    {거른보기.length > 0 && (
      <div class="scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Company</th>
              <th>Ticker</th>
              <th class="num">Stated tenure</th>
              <th class="num">Company age</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {거른보기.map((r: any) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{r.회사 ?? <span class="dim">name not in our list</span>}</td>
                <td class="dim">{r.ticker}</td>
                <td class="num">{해(r.햇수)}</td>
                <td class="num">{r.회사나이 == null ? '—' : `${Number(r.회사나이).toFixed(1)} years`}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    )}
    <p class="note">
      Our own article on this data,
      {' '}<a href={f._옆지면?.주소 ?? '/article/korea-ceo-tenure-eleven-year-median'}>
        Korea's listed CEOs: the median has run the company eleven years</a>, set aside 148
      companies on the same test. It counted one chief executive per company — the
      longest-serving where there are several — and reached a median of 11.0 years. This page
      counts every registered seat and reaches {해(f.분위?.중앙)}. <b>Both numbers are right
      for what they count</b>, and we print them side by side rather than quietly choosing one.
    </p>

    <h2>The distribution, not the average</h2>
    <p>
      An average would put a single number on {N(f.잰수)} very different careers, and a
      single number read as a norm stops being a map and starts being a push. So here is
      the whole spread. The largest band is <b>{가장큰칸?.이름}</b> at
      {' '}{N(가장큰칸?.수)} people, but it holds only {pct(가장큰칸?.몫)} of the total —
      no band holds even a quarter.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Tenure</th>
            <th class="num">CEOs</th>
            <th class="num">Share</th>
            <th>Of those we could read</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {칸.map((c: any) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{c.이름}</td>
              <td class="num">{N(c.수)}</td>
              <td class="num">{pct(c.몫)}</td>
              <td>
                <span class="bar" style={`width:${((c.몫 ?? 0) * 100 * 3.6).toFixed(1)}%`}></span>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Bands include the lower bound and exclude the upper one, so a CEO at exactly twenty
      years sits in the 20–30 row. Percentages are of the {N(f.잰수)} tenures we could read,
      not of all {N(f.대표수)} chief executives.
    </p>

    <h2>Both tails are crowded</h2>
    <p>
      The common shorthand is that Korean listed companies are owner-led and their chief
      executives stay for decades. {N(f.스물넘은수)} of them — {pct(스물몫)} — have indeed
      held the seat twenty years or longer. But at the same time
      {' '}<b>{N(삼년밑)} ({pct(삼년밑몫)}) have held it under three years</b>. The quartiles
      say the same thing: {해(f.분위?.p25)} at the first, {해(f.분위?.p75)} at the third.
      This is not one population with a typical length. It is two groups sharing a table.
    </p>

    <h2>Full-time and part-time are not the same job</h2>
    <p>
      The filings mark whether the executive serves full-time. Among those we could measure,
      the full-time median is <b>{해(f.상근대비?.상근?.중앙)}</b> against
      {' '}<b>{해(f.상근대비?.비상근?.중앙)}</b> for the
      {' '}{N(f.상근대비?.비상근?.전체)} chief executives recorded as not full-time
      ({N(f.상근대비?.비상근?.잰수)} of whom stated a readable tenure). That is a gap of
      years, not months — and it means any single median for "the Korean CEO" is averaging
      across two different arrangements.
    </p>

    <h2>The longest-serving</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Ranked by stated tenure, not by company size. Ties are left in filing order; we do not
      break them.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Company</th>
            <th>Ticker</th>
            <th>Chief executive</th>
            <th class="num">Tenure</th>
            <th>Full-time</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {오래.map((r: any) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{r.회사 ?? <span class="dim">name not in our list</span>}</td>
              <td class="dim">{r.ticker}</td>
              <td>{r.사람 ?? <span class="dim">—</span>}</td>
              <td class="num">{해(r.햇수)}</td>
              <td class="dim">{r.상근인가 ? 'Yes' : 'No'}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Romanised names are our transliteration of the Korean filing, and may differ from the
      spelling the person uses. Company names come from the regulator's own English register;
      where a ticker is missing from it we say so rather than inventing a name.
    </p>

    <h2 class="warn-h">What this page does not tell you</h2>
    <div class="warn">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <b>Whether long tenure is good or bad.</b> Stability and entrenchment produce the
          same number. We counted years in the seat; we did not grade them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>How Korea compares.</b> We have not measured chief-executive tenure in any other
          market, so we do not put one here. A figure we did not count is not a figure we
          will print.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Who holds seats at more than one company.</b> The filings carry no birth date,
          so two identical names may be one person or two. We do not merge them, and we do
          not count concurrent appointments at all.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>What the {N(f.못잰수)} unmeasured CEOs look like.</b> They may skew long or
          short. Leaving them out of the percentages is the honest option, not a neutral one,
          and we flag it rather than hide it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Which of the {N(f.거른수)} set-aside rows are wrong.</b> A re-incorporation and
          a bad join look identical from here. We removed them from the distribution because
          we cannot verify them, not because we know they are false.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Anything about one company from this distribution.</b> It is a shape across
          {' '}{N(f.회사수)} firms. A shape is not a statement about any single seat.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="note">
      Source: {f._출처}. Tenure is the figure the company itself filed; we did not recompute
      it from appointment dates. Every number on this page is computed at build time from
      <code>ceo-tenure.json</code> by <code>scripts/measure-ceo-tenure.mjs</code>; none is
      transcribed by hand. Rows whose tenure we could not read are reported as unmeasured.
    </p>

    <BuyBar />
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .wrap { max-width: 56rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem 1rem 3rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1.25; margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.12rem; margin: 1.8rem 0 .5rem; }
  h2.warn-h { color: var(--warn, #9a3412); }
  .lead { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }
  p { line-height: 1.65; }
  .stats {
    display: grid; gap: .6rem; margin: 1rem 0 1.4rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(9rem, 1fr));
  }
  .stat { padding: .7rem .8rem; border: 1px solid var(--line, #e5e5e5); border-radius: 6px; }
  .stat b { display: block; font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.2; }
  .stat span { font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted, #666); }
  .warn {
    padding: .8rem .95rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent, #0f4c81);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent, #0f4c81) 6%, transparent);
  }
  .note { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted, #555); }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .85rem; margin: .6rem 0; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: .45rem .55rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line, #eee); }
  th { font-weight: 650; white-space: nowrap; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  td.dim, span.dim { color: var(--muted, #666); white-space: nowrap; }
  .bar {
    display: inline-block; height: .55rem; min-width: 1px; border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--accent, #0f4c81); opacity: .55; vertical-align: middle;
  }
  ul { line-height: 1.65; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  ul li { margin-bottom: .45rem; }
  code { font-size: .9em; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .stat { border-color: #333; }
    h2.warn-h { color: #fdba74; }
    td.dim, span.dim, .note, .stat span { color: #aaa; }
  }
</style>
